// === PREAMBLE ===
// @trope    Rousing Speech
// @category Oratory / Persuasion
// @source   https://allthetropes.org/wiki/Rousing_Speech
// @version  1.3
//
// Laconic (per the wiki): a speech that inspires courage and resolve — a leader transforming the
// fear of the outnumbered and disheartened into the willingness to fight. FRONTIER: the BRIGHT
// MIRROR of propaganda. Both run low on logos (you cannot argue a frightened army into courage),
// but where propaganda stokes fear of a SCAPEGOAT and seats a lie, the rousing speech appeals to
// shared HONOR and BELONGING and seats a truth the listeners already hold — and it galvanizes
// directly to ACTION, skipping belief-change entirely. It is also in-DIEGETIC persuasion: a
// character moving a group of characters, the speaker↔audience machinery run one level down.

import "trl/modules/persuasion.trl"          // the machinery, honest and in-diegesis

assoc rousing_speech -> [
  persuasion : "is the honest, pathos-only end of",
  propaganda : "is the bright mirror of (honor where it stokes fear)",
  needs      : "rallies the belonging and esteem rungs of"
]

imply RousingSpeech -> [Pathos, Resolve, Narrative]

// Naming rule: a leader who appeals to shared honor turns a disheartened band's fear into resolve —
// no argument, no lie, only the calling-up of what they already are.
rule Rousing_Speech {
  when:
    char $s [+Leader]
    evt  $r [&Rallies(agent=$s, band=$g, cause=$cause)]
    $g [#Disheartened]
  then:
    $g [-Disheartened]
    $g [+Resolved(to=$cause)]
    $g -- resolve
}

// === CONCRETE VIGNETTE: Henry V, the St. Crispin's Day speech — Agincourt (Shakespeare, 1599) ===
// Outnumbered perhaps five to one, the English are sick, soaked, and sure they will die. Henry does
// not argue the odds — he reframes the few as the privileged: "We few, we happy few, we band of
// brothers." The fear does not vanish because the danger changed; it is displaced by a thing the
// men want more than safety — to be of that band. They resolve to fight.
char henry [+Leader]
set  the_english [#Disheartened]

scene before_agincourt {
  beat 1 {
    evt st_crispins_day [&Rallies(agent=henry, band=the_english, cause=brotherhood)]
    // Rousing_Speech -> the_english [-Disheartened] [+Resolved(to=brotherhood)] -- resolve
  }
}
